slides.content:
# Using Your Own Fonts

```jsx
import localFont from 'next/font/local';

const myFont = localFont({
  src: './fonts/MyFont.woff2',
  weight: '400',
});
```

Variable fonts: if your font is variable, you can specify multiple weights without multiple files.

```jsx
const inter = Inter({ subsets: ['latin'], variable: '--font-inter' });
// then use `--font-inter` in CSS
```

This gives you both the class name and a CSS variable for custom selectors.

